      { q: "What does Shaana’s last postcard tell us about her feelings?", a: "She is happy to be home but misses the forests, glaciers, deserts and people. She hopes to travel again and take her friends along next time.", marks: 3 },
      { q: "Case: Veer’s family visits a snowy hill in January and a beach in June. He keeps a travel diary describing the cold, the snow and later the warm waves. (i) Which text does this remind you of? (ii) What does Veer learn about different regions? (iii) Why is keeping such a record useful?", a: "(i) ‘North, South, East, West’. (ii) That regions differ in climate and landscape. (iii) It records his experiences and helps him share and remember them.", marks: 4, type: "case" }
